stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Admission: request attempt
    Admission --> Refused: invalid or untrusted inputs
    Admission --> Starting: admitted profile and attempt ID
    Starting --> Measuring: observed readiness
    Starting --> Capturing: settled startup failure, retain available facts
    Starting --> Retained: producer unsettled
    Measuring --> Capturing: finish / cancel / deadline
    Capturing --> Exporting: close window, capture and drain settled
    Capturing --> Retained: deadline, producer unsettled
    Exporting --> Retained: failed or incomplete export
    Exporting --> Cleanup: original bytes retained and verified
    Retained --> Exporting: explicit recovery after observed settlement
    Cleanup --> LifecycleComplete: owned resources observed released
    Cleanup --> Unknown: cleanup or native outcome unknown
    Refused --> [*]
    LifecycleComplete --> [*]
    Unknown --> [*]
    note right of Retained
        A finite supervisor bounds owned work.
        Preserve closed bytes and durable record;
        the attempt may exit for later recovery.
        Never repeat the measurement.
    end note
    note right of Unknown
        Lifecycle completion is separate from
        native outcome and assessment verdict.
        A process exit does not prove physical stopping.
    end note
